---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ThemeToggle from '../components/ThemeToggle.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SOURCE_URL } from '../lib/config';
---

<Layout
	title="Grade Viewer is shutting down"
	description="Grade Viewer is no longer available. This independent project has been discontinued."
>
	<header class="border-b border-border">
		<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-3xl items-center justify-between gap-3 px-4 py-3">
			<p class="font-medium">Grade Viewer</p>
			<div class="flex items-center gap-2">
				<ThemeToggle />
				<a
					class="inline-flex h-8 items-center gap-1.5 rounded px-2.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground no-underline hover:bg-muted hover:text-foreground"
					href={SOURCE_URL}
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>
					<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
						<path d="M12 2C6.477 2 2 6.477 2 12c0 4.42 2.865 8.17 6.839 9.49.5.092.682-.217.682-.482 0-.237-.008-.866-.013-1.7-2.782.603-3.369-1.342-3.369-1.342-.454-1.155-1.11-1.462-1.11-1.462-.908-.62.069-.608.069-.608 1.003.07 1.531 1.03 1.531 1.03.892 1.529 2.341 1.087 2.91.832.092-.647.35-1.088.636-1.338-2.22-.253-4.555-1.11-4.555-4.943 0-1.091.39-1.984 1.029-2.683-.103-.253-.446-1.27.098-2.647 0 0 .84-.269 2.75 1.025A9.58 9.58 0 0 1 12 6.836c.85.004 1.705.114 2.504.336 1.909-1.294 2.747-1.025 2.747-1.025.546 1.377.203 2.394.1 2.647.64.699 1.028 1.592 1.028 2.683 0 3.842-2.339 4.687-4.566 4.935.359.309.678.919.678 1.852 0 1.336-.012 2.415-.012 2.743 0 .267.18.578.688.48C19.138 20.167 22 16.418 22 12c0-5.523-4.477-10-10-10z" />
					</svg>
					Source
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</header>

	<main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl flex-1 px-4 pt-12 pb-20">
		<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">August 31, 2026</p>
		<h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Grade Viewer is shutting down</h1>
		<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			Sign-in is off. This site no longer connects to any school district system, and it no longer
			collects a login. If this browser had a saved sign-in, it is being deleted now.
		</p>

		<section class="mt-10 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			<h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-foreground">What this was</h2>
			<p>
				Grade Viewer was a small, independent, open-source website. It ran in your browser and let
				you look at grades, mail, attendance, and documents you could already see in your school’s
				official portal, plus local what-if scores that never left this device. It was not a district
				product. It was not for profit. It was never affiliated with, endorsed by, or approved by
				Edupoint Educational Systems or any school.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-10 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			<h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-foreground">The letter</h2>
			<p>
				On August 31, 2026, Edupoint Educational Systems emailed
				{' '}<a class="underline" href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
				Edupoint makes the student information system many schools use, and it owns the federally
				registered EDUPOINT, SYNERGY, and STUDENTVUE trademarks. They asked us to stop, and to
				confirm in writing by September 8, 2026. We are complying.
			</p>
			<p>They raised two issues.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-10 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			<h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-foreground">1. Their trademarks</h2>
			<p>
				They agreed the product name “Grade Viewer” does not include their marks, and that the
				project said it was not affiliated with them. Their concern was narrower: the site described
				itself <em>as</em> a viewer for their product. The homepage headline, body copy, and search
				description used their mark as the main way to explain what this was. They say that can make
				people think Grade Viewer is associated with, endorsed by, or approved by Edupoint.
			</p>
			<p>
				We are removing that marketing use: it is gone from this homepage, from page metadata, and
				from the other public pages on this site.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-10 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			<h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-foreground">2. Connecting to their systems</h2>
			<p>
				Grade Viewer asked you for the same username and password you already use at school, then
				your <em>browser</em> used those to load records from Edupoint’s web services. We did not
				keep a password or gradebook on our servers. After sign-in, this device kept an encrypted
				copy of the login; signing out deleted it.
			</p>
			<p>
				Edupoint’s position is that those measures do not matter for permission. They say they never
				authorized this application to connect, that a student cannot grant that permission on
				Edupoint’s behalf, and that the access itself is unauthorized. They cited student-privacy
				and computer-access laws as concerns, including FERPA, COPPA, the Computer Fraud and Abuse
				Act, and state unfair-trade-practice laws.
			</p>
			<p>
				We are not going to litigate that on this page. We are stopping the connection.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-10 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			<h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-foreground">What they asked us to do</h2>
			<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
				<li>Stop using their marks in the app name, domain, repository, listings, metadata, and marketing.</li>
				<li>Stop all access to and use of their web services and systems.</li>
				<li>
					Destroy data belonging to others that we obtained by building or running this app,
					including stored logins and usage identifiers derived from them.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-10 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			<h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-foreground">What we are doing</h2>
			<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
				<li>Sign-in, grades, mail, attendance, and documents are turned off.</li>
				<li>This site will not contact Edupoint systems.</li>
				<li>Any encrypted login saved in <em>this</em> browser is deleted when you open this page.</li>
				<li>We will delete hashed usage IDs that were stored only to count unique sign-ins.</li>
				<li>We never had a server-side copy of passwords or gradebooks to delete.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Use your school’s official portal for grades and school mail. That is the supported way to
				see the same information.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-10 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			<h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-foreground">Questions</h2>
			<p>
				Email
				{' '}<a class="underline" href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
				The source remains publicly available.
			</p>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
